<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan CK group buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CK group buys 54,000T U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's CK group bought one 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Agrex at a tender on Wednesday, but passed on another 54,000-tonne shipment, traders said.  </p>
<p>The CK Group comprises Chia Hsin Flour Feed and Vegetable Oil Corp and some buyers from Taiwan's southern port city of Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>Traders said the shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Shipment Tonnes Date/Location		   Price/Futures</p>
<p>		     U.S. Gulf Pacific Northwest</p>
<p>   One    33,500 Sept 5-20 Sept 21-Oct 5     $121.80</p>
<p>   One    20,500 Sept 5-20 Sept 21-Oct 5     80.37 US cnets/Sep</p>
<p>   Two    54,000 Oct  5-20 Oct  21-Nov 5     passed</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
